				"README.md": {
					"diff": "--- published/README.md\n+++ rebuilt/README.md\n@@ -1,101 +1,197 @@\n-# i18n Tools (React)\n+# 🎨 Spor: Vy's Design System\n \n-Here, you'll find tools for handling internationalization of your apps, and for all components in the `spor-react` component library.\n+Welcome to **Spor**, Vy's open-source design system! Spor is a **shared language for designers and developers**, helping us build **consistent, accessible, and high-quality user experiences** across all platforms.\n \n-## Installation\n+## 📖 Table of Contents\n \n-```bash\n-$ npm install @vygruppen/spor-i18n-react\n-```\n+- [What is Spor?](#-what-is-spor)\n+- [Repository Structure](#-repository-structure)\n+- [Getting Started](#-getting-started)\n+- [How to Contribute](#-how-to-contribute)\n+- [Design System Fundamentals](#-design-system-fundamentals)\n+- [Accessibility](#-accessibility)\n+- [Releasing New Versions](#-releasing-new-versions)\n+- [Adding New Icons](#-adding-new-icons)\n+- [Additional Resources](#-additional-resources)\n \n-## Usage\n+---\n \n-```tsx\n-import {\n-  Language,\n-  LanguageProvider,\n-  useTranslation,\n-  Translations,\n-} from \"@vygruppen/spor-i18n-react\";\n-```\n+## 📌 What is Spor?\n \n-The first thing you need to do, is to wrap your application in a `LanguageProvider`. If you're using the `SporProvider` from `@vygruppen/spor-react`, this is already done for you.\n+Spor provides:\n \n-The `LanguageProvider` requires you to specify a `language` prop with a value from the `Language` enum.\n+- **Reusable UI components** for web and mobile\n+- **Design tokens** for colors, typography, spacing, and more\n+- **Guidelines and documentation** for usage and best practices\n+- **A collaborative space** for designers and developers to contribute\n \n-```tsx\n-import { Language, LanguageProvider } from \"@vygruppen/spor-i18n-react\";\n+Our goal is to ensure **visual and functional consistency** across Vy's digital products. Anyone—inside or outside Vy—can contribute! 🚀\n \n-const Root = () => (\n-  <LanguageProvider language={Language.English}>\n-    <App />\n-  </LanguageProvider>\n-);\n-```\n+---\n \n-> ### Supported languages\n->\n-> Currently, we support Norwegian (bokmål), Swedish and English. If you need other languages, please contact the Spor team.\n-\n-It's up to you to specify and handle any \"current language\" state, either by getting it from an API, or saving it in local storage, for instance.\n-\n-Once you've done this, you can now translate strings easily. Let's move to an example component.\n-\n-```tsx\n-const ExampleComponent = () => {\n-  return <Box>I need to be translated</Box>;\n-};\n-```\n+## 📂 Repository Structure\n+\n+Spor follows a **monorepo** structure, containing multiple **packages** and **applications**.\n+\n+### 🚀 Applications\n+\n+- **`designmanual-frontend`** – A Remix app for documentation and demos (this site).\n+- **`design-studio`** – A Sanity Studio app for managing documentation ([spor.vy.no/studio](https://spor.vy.no/studio)).\n+\n+### 📦 Key Packages\n+\n+- **`@vygruppen/spor-react`** – The React component library.\n+- **`@vygruppen/spor-design-tokens`** – Design tokens (colors, typography, spacing, etc.).\n+- **`@vygruppen/spor-icon`** – SVG icons.\n+- **`@vygruppen/spor-icon-react`** – React components for icons.\n+- **`@vygruppen/spor-icon-react-native`** – React Native components for icons.\n+- **`@vygruppen/spor-loader`** – All Lottie loading animation data.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 🔧 Getting Started\n+\n+### ✅ Prerequisites\n+\n+Before you begin, ensure you have:\n+\n+- **Node.js** installed.\n+- **Basic familiarity with Git** for version control.\n",
